<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Western African Ebola epidemic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2013–2016</span> · Also known as West African Ebola epidemic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Western African Ebola epidemic was the largest outbreak of Ebola virus disease on record, spreading from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> in late 2013 to Liberia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a>. It caused more than 28,000 cases and over 11,000 deaths, nearly 5,000 of them in Liberia, closing schools and halting much economic life before it was brought under control in 2016.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/western-african-ebola-epidemic.jpg" alt="Western African Ebola epidemic" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ZeLonewolf · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2014_ebola_virus_epidemic_in_West_Africa_simplified.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
